---
export const prerender = true
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro"
import DocCallout from "../../components/docs/DocCallout.astro"
import DocCode from "../../components/docs/DocCode.astro"
import DocRelated from "../../components/docs/DocRelated.astro"
import { stack } from "../../data/architecture"

const toc = [
  { title: "Choices", href: "#choices" },
  { title: "Pins", href: "#pins" },
  { title: "Effect shape", href: "#effect" },
  { title: "Why a sidecar", href: "#sidecar" },
  { title: "Units", href: "#units" },
  { title: "Boundaries", href: "#boundaries" },
]
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Stack"
  subtitle="One Effect pin, one SQLite writer, SolidJS in the webview, Rust around the window."
  description="CADCAMFUN stack pins: Bun, Effect 4.0.0-rc.112, Drizzle, Tauri v2, SolidJS, nikcli."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="choices" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Choices</h2>
    <p>
      Spec <code>00-overview.md</code> §1 fixes the stack. The previous Next.js, Prisma, and
      Stripe codebase stays in <code>.reference/</code>, git-ignored and read-only. Use it for
      domain knowledge. Do not import from it.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Concern</th><th>Choice</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {stack.map((row) => (
          <tr><td>{row.concern}</td><td>{row.choice}</td></tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      The UI packages are <code>solid-js</code>, <code>@solidjs/router</code>, and
      <code>vite-plugin-solid</code>. Spec 06 re-implements the legacy React screens in Solid.
      Three.js draws the viewport. Tailwind is the styling layer. Tests for screens use
      <code>@solidjs/testing-library</code>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="pins" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Pins</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Package</th><th>Version in this repo</th><th>Where</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Bun</td><td><code>1.4.2</code> (<code>packageManager</code>)</td><td>root <code>package.json</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>effect</code></td><td><code>4.0.0-rc.112</code></td><td>workspace-wide; required by nikcli</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>drizzle-orm</code> / <code>drizzle-kit</code></td><td><code>1.0.0-beta.22</code></td><td><code>packages/db/package.json</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>@nikcli-ai/sdk-next</code></td><td><code>1.428.0</code></td><td><code>packages/ai/package.json</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>App</td><td><code>6.0.0</code></td><td>root <code>package.json</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <DocCallout type="warn" title="Do not bump Effect in one package">
      <p>
        <code>@nikcli-ai/sdk-next</code> requires <code>4.0.0-rc.112</code>. One copy keeps
        <code>Context</code> tags identical across Layers. Version-matched docs are
        <code>node_modules/effect/ai-docs/src/</code> inside a workspace package (Bun does not hoist).
        Those docs differ from Effect v3. Read the folder that matches the API you are calling
        before writing Effect code.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
    <p>
      HTTP server examples for this pin live in
      <code>node_modules/effect/ai-docs/src/51_http-server/</code> (<code>10_basics.ts</code> and
      <code>fixtures/</code>). Sidecar imports are <code>effect/http</code>,
      <code>effect/http-api</code>, and <code>@effect/platform-bun</code>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="effect" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Effect shape</h2>
    <p>
      Services are classes. The tag string is <code>cadcamfun/X</code>. Traced functions use
      <code>Effect.fn("Module.name")</code>. Hot paths use <code>Effect.fnUntraced</code>. Errors
      that cross HTTP are <code>Schema.TaggedError</code>. Internal-only errors may use
      <code>Data.TaggedError</code>. External input is decoded with
      <code>Schema.decodeUnknownEffect</code>.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="ts" title="Service tag used in this repo">
{`class Database extends Context.Service<Database, Shape>()("cadcamfun/Database") {
  static layer = ...
}`}
    </DocCode>
    <p>
      Tags present in tree include <code>cadcamfun/Database</code>
      (<code>packages/db/src/index.ts</code>) and <code>cadcamfun/AppConfig</code>
      (<code>apps/sidecar/src/config.ts</code>). Spec 08 defines
      <code>cadcamfun/AiCredentials</code> and <code>cadcamfun/AiService</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Resources use <code>Effect.acquireRelease</code> inside a Layer. Callers never close the
      SQLite handle. Tests are plain <code>bun:test</code>. Run an effect with
      <code>Effect.runPromise</code> and provide layers explicitly. Database tests use
      <code>:memory:</code> SQLite.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="sidecar" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Why a sidecar</h2>
    <p>
      Persistence is <code>bun:sqlite</code> plus Drizzle in the same process as Effect. An
      Electron main process is Node and has no <code>bun:sqlite</code>. Tauri leaves application
      logic in a compiled Bun binary. The Rust shell stays on window, tray, menus, updater,
      keychain, and process lifecycle. Rust 1.96 is the toolchain named in spec 07. The CLI is
      <code>bunx tauri</code> from <code>apps/desktop</code>.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="bash" title="Dev window (root package.json)">
{`bun run desktop:dev
# build:sidecar, then @cadcamfun/desktop tauri dev`}
    </DocCode>
    <p>
      Packaged builds are <code>bun run build</code>, <code>bun run build:sidecar</code>, and
      <code>bun run build:desktop</code>. The reproducible pipeline is <code>scripts/build.ts</code>
      (spec 10).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="units" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Units</h2>
    <p>
      Internal geometry and CAM use millimetres and radians. Convert at the UI or the G-code
      boundary. Angles in degrees never cross a module boundary. G-code numbers use a fixed
      decimal count. The post default is 3 (<code>PostOptions.decimals</code> in
      <code>packages/core/src/cam/post/types.ts</code>). Display conversion for the viewport lives
      in <code>apps/desktop/src/viewport/units.ts</code> (<code>toDisplay</code>,
      <code>fromDisplay</code>, <code>formatLength</code>, <code>formatAngle</code>).
    </p>
    <p>
      AI provider keys are configuration the user supplies, and they are kept out of process
      environment variables used for the model. Spec 05 and spec 08 put them in the OS keychain
      and in an owner-only file <code>&lt;data dir&gt;/ai/credentials.json</code> (mode 0600).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="boundaries" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Boundaries</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Hot geometry and CAM loops in <code>packages/core</code> are plain functions. Effect and Schema wrap them at the edges.</li>
      <li>A single package must not bump <code>effect</code> on its own. The pin moves for the whole workspace when <code>sdk-next</code> moves.</li>
      <li>The desktop must not open <code>bun:sqlite</code>. The sidecar is the process that does.</li>
      <li>The Rust shell must not grow toolpath math, solid kernels, or Drizzle queries.</li>
      <li><code>.env*</code> files at the repo root are legacy. v6 does not read them. Agents must not print their values.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <DocRelated items={[{ title: "Conventions", href: "/docs/conventions" }, { title: "Database", href: "/docs/database" }, { title: "Architecture", href: "/docs/architecture" }]} />
</DocsLayout>
